---
import { issuesUrl, repositoryUrl } from "../data/site";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout title="About MathMyRate: Free Rate and Fee Calculators" description="What MathMyRate is and is not: free, browser-based pricing and payment-fee calculators with officially sourced fee rules, and no accounts or paywalls.">
  <main id="main-content" class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-16 md:px-8 md:py-24">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1 class="display mt-4 text-5xl font-bold leading-none md:text-6xl">A calculator, not an oracle.</h1>
    <div class="guide mt-10 text-lg">
      <p>MathMyRate is a free suite of pricing calculators for freelancers and digital-product sellers. It answers two practical questions, what to charge and what you keep, with the assumptions attached, so you can disagree with the inputs instead of the tool.</p>
      <h2>Who runs it</h2>
      <p>MathMyRate is an independent project. It is not affiliated with, sponsored by, or endorsed by Stripe, PayPal, Gumroad, Lemon Squeezy, or any other provider it covers. The complete source code, including every fee rule and the tests that check it, is public on <a href={repositoryUrl}>GitHub</a>.</p>
      <h2>How the numbers are made</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Fee rules come only from each provider's own pricing and help pages. Every fee calculator links its sources and shows the date they were last reviewed.</li>
        <li>Calculations use integer-cent arithmetic. The worked examples and tables on each page come from the same code as the calculator.</li>
        <li>Cases the sources do not document are labeled unsupported instead of estimated.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>The <a href="/methodology/">methodology page</a> explains rounding, sourcing, and review in detail, and the <a href="/changelog/">changelog</a> lists every fee rule change.</p>
      <h2>Corrections</h2>
      <p>If a result disagrees with a provider's current pricing, or with the assumptions a page states, please <a href={issuesUrl}>open an issue on GitHub</a>. Include the page, the numbers you entered, and the official page you compared against. Issues are public, so leave out any private financial details.</p>
      <h2>What this is not</h2>
      <p>It is not a tax, accounting, legal, or financial advice service. Results are estimates that depend on the inputs you provide. For decisions that matter, talk to a qualified professional who knows your situation.</p>
      <h2>How it is paid for</h2>
      <p>Every calculator is free, with no accounts and no paywalls. The site shows no advertising today. If advertising is added later, the <a href="/privacy/">privacy page</a> will name the ad providers, what they collect, and your consent choices before any ad appears.</p>
      <h2>How it is built</h2>
      <p>The site is a static build. Calculations run in your browser and are not sent to a server.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
